# Conventional Commits (single line)

Every commit message is exactly **one line** in the format:

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <description>
```

## Rules

- Single line only: no body, no footer, no trailers (no `Co-authored-by`, no `Signed-off-by`).
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `test`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`.
- Scope (optional) is the affected area: `domain`, `app`, `http`, `repo`, `cmd`, etc.
- Description: imperative mood, lowercase start, no trailing period, max ~72 chars total.
- Breaking change: add `!` after type/scope, e.g. `feat(http)!: change ingest payload shape`.
- Commit small, focused changes often; one logical change per commit.
- Use `git commit -m "<message>"` with a single `-m` only.

## Examples

```
✅ test(domain): add failing test for membership expiry after two weeks
✅ feat(app): implement segment estimation use case
✅ feat(http): add POST /memberships inbound adapter
✅ refactor(repo): extract ttl calculation into helper
✅ docs: explain choice of REST for ingestion

❌ Added estimation feature.
❌ feat: Implement Estimator
❌ fix: bug fix

   Detailed body lines...
```
